  ('mth-208-numerical-analysis', 'MTH 208: Numerical Analysis', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the inverse of $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\ 3 & 2 & 2 \\ 1 & 2 & 3 \end{pmatrix}$ using the adjoint method.', '["$\\begin{pmatrix} -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$", "$\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}$", "$\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\end{pmatrix}$", "$\\begin{pmatrix} -2 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'With $\det A = \pm1$, computing cofactors, transposing to form the adjoint, and dividing by $\det A$ gives $A^{-1} = $\begin{pmatrix} -2 & 1 & 0 \\ 7 & -2 & -1 \\ -4 & 1 & 1 \end{pmatrix}$$, verified by $AA^{-1}=I$.', 'Inverse of a Matrix', false, 'second', 2),
