  ('mth-208-numerical-analysis', 'MTH 208: Numerical Analysis', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the inverse of $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & -2 \\ -2 & -4 & 3 \\ 0 & -1 & 2 \end{pmatrix}$ using the adjoint method.', '["$\\begin{pmatrix} 5 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$", "$\\begin{pmatrix} -5 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$", "$\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\end{pmatrix}$", "$\\begin{pmatrix} 5 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'With $\det A = \pm1$, computing cofactors, transposing to form the adjoint, and dividing by $\det A$ gives $A^{-1} = $\begin{pmatrix} 5 & 2 & 2 \\ -4 & -2 & -1 \\ -2 & -1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}$$, verified by $AA^{-1}=I$.', 'Inverse of a Matrix', false, 'second', 2),
