  ('mth-208-numerical-analysis', 'MTH 208: Numerical Analysis', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the inverse of $\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -2 & 3 \\ -2 & -1 & 4 \\ -3 & 2 & 1 \end{pmatrix}$ using the adjoint method.', '["$\\begin{pmatrix} 9 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 10 & -9 & 6 \\\\ 7 & -6 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}$", "$\\begin{pmatrix} -9 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -10 & 9 & -6 \\\\ -7 & 6 & -4 \\end{pmatrix}$", "$\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$", "$\\begin{pmatrix} 9 & 10 & 7 \\\\ -8 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'With $\det A = \pm1$, computing cofactors, transposing to form the adjoint, and dividing by $\det A$ gives $A^{-1} = $\begin{pmatrix} 9 & -8 & 5 \\ 10 & -9 & 6 \\ 7 & -6 & 4 \end{pmatrix}$$, verified by $AA^{-1}=I$.', 'Inverse of a Matrix', false, 'second', 2),
